cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AdjAgent: an evidence-grounded agent harness for vaccine adjuvant research"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Xinming
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Yi
version: release-v0.1
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gudehhh666/AdjAgent"
abstract: >-
  AdjAgent is an agent harness for vaccine adjuvant research that separates
  decision from verification. One host service and one agent loop share a tool
  catalog; the host creates every source, binds claims to retrieved passages,
  gates citations and ranks experiments, while the model plans and writes. The
  harness integrates typed resource packs, a local literature library and
  sandboxed computation; binds answers and reports to evidence; and compares
  competing mechanism hypotheses as a graph with edge-level citation gating and
  value-per-cost experiment ranking.
keywords:
  - scientific agents
  - large language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - citation verification
  - vaccine adjuvants
